question_en:
What does the following C function print when called with the head of the list 1 → 2 → 3 → 4?

void f(struct node *p) {
  if (p == NULL) return;
  f(p->next);
  printf("%d ", p->data);
}

What value does f(7) return?

int f(int n) {
  if (n <= 1) return 1;
  return n * f(n - 2);
}

What is printed by the call p(3)?

void p(int n) {
  if (n == 0) return;
  printf("%d ", n);
  p(n - 1);
  printf("%d ", n);
}

What is the time complexity of the following code?

for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
  for (j = 0; j < n; j++)
    sum = sum + a[i][j];

What is the time complexity of this loop?

for (i = 1; i < n; i = i * 2)
  count++;

What is the time complexity of the following code?

for (i = 1; i <= n; i++)
  for (j = 1; j <= n; j = j * 2)
    count++;
